# Lurrus of the Dream-Den: "Once during each of your turns, you may cast a permanent spell with mana value 2 or less from your
# graveyard." Bot1's graveyard holds a Cathar Commando (flash, so only the turn restriction stops it). On Bot2's turn 2 it
# cannot be cast (the refusal); on Bot1's turn 3 it can (the positive control). On Bot2's turn 4 Bot2 cannot cast the Mox Pearl in its
# own graveyard: Lurrus's permission is Bot1's alone (the refusal). Faithless Looting puts the Commando there on turn 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Faithless Looting
Lurrus of the Dream-Den
Plains
Cathar Commando
Plains
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Mox Pearl
Island x12

